  {
   "text": "{\"explanations\":[{\"signal_id\":\"fee41730-fa44-40e3-913b-5ed2f99d9974\",\"explanation\":\"Runway stands at {{fact:07b61f82-22e1-414c-b86a-41bc7d9627c7}} months at October 31, so at the current burn the cash on hand would be exhausted in well under a year. This is the core repayment concern, and the cash covenant shortfall and the shrinking runway covenant cushion both point the same way.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"0ecb9844-f457-4a75-a80f-3be6e5228e3c\",\"explanation\":\"Unrestricted cash of {{fact:72314421-976e-4db8-8c1a-54edfb96cefd}} is below the covenant minimum of {{fact:90263cfa-801d-4997-8049-daccf4de5980}}, leaving headroom of {{fact:420db624-0e32-49de-bd64-e9d3d4a80144}}. The cushion is not just thin but negative, which reads as the covenant level being crossed. It is the balance-sheet side of the short runway.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"95c43fe5-773b-4d29-b0f9-54d5bfb030c9\",\"explanation\":\"Cash covenant headroom has fallen steadily, from {{fact:741f3e4a-e75a-45fa-a96d-a724bb5bbbdd}} in August to {{fact:27f2a252-f5c7-43cc-b69c-5b44d45a368b}} in September and {{fact:420db624-0e32-49de-bd64-e9d3d4a80144}} in October. The trend shows the shortfall is a sustained cash drain rather than a one-month dip, which reinforces the runway concern.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"9f70fe6b-26b3-4dc1-8b43-301ab7e90827\",\"explanation\":\"Runway covenant headroom has narrowed from {{fact:d69d82c4-2686-4c71-a085-bde0ef4a0246}} in August to {{fact:0f4a516c-80bb-4a2d-90d8-840c4dc82c95}} in September and {{fact:fd556cd6-994a-4d89-9e88-46a9b164bf2d}} in October. Runway of {{fact:487a261a-74e2-4da2-b28a-9a21c7314a68}} months is still above the minimum of {{fact:4ade100d-b734-4ee7-b218-8cfac3d30ff0}}, but at this pace the cushion could disappear soon, mirroring the cash covenant's path.\"}],\"ranking\":[\"fee41730-fa44-40e3-913b-5ed2f99d9974\",\"0ecb9844-f457-4a75-a80f-3be6e5228e3c\",\"95c43fe5-773b-4d29-b0f9-54d5bfb030c9\",\"9f70fe6b-26b3-4dc1-8b43-301ab7e90827\"]}",
